{"path":"results/simple-ideas-10x10-p2-5-len4g3-comp0-7-bounties-from-5-alpha-beta-20261023/summary.md","title":"Hard graph (10 × 10, long sequences): α × β","html":"<h1>Hard graph (10 × 10, long sequences): α × β</h1>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> On a hard idea graph (10 levels × 10, 2.5 parents, sequences of 4 bits growing by 3, bounties from level 5), how do α and β decide how far a society gets?</p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Best overall: OSO (α = 0.2, β = 1). Against traditional, clearly better on hardest level, targets solved, bounty value, ROI, knowledge found (bits), knowledge per unit of money and waste. (8 measures; a clear difference is more than 2.7 standard errors.)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>hardest level: 8.80 against traditional 1.77, clearly better.</li>\n<li>targets solved: 6.05 against traditional 0.38, clearly better.</li>\n<li>bounty value: 1350 against traditional 26, clearly better.</li>\n<li>ROI: 0.23 against traditional 0.00, clearly better.</li>\n<li>knowledge found (bits): 317 against traditional 133, clearly better.</li>\n<li>knowledge per unit of money: 0.05 against traditional 0.02, clearly better.</li>\n<li>money to the main level: best α = 0.8, β = 0.75, 2592.</li>\n<li>waste: 0.17 against traditional 0.55, clearly better.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img src=\"files/results/simple-ideas-10x10-p2-5-len4g3-comp0-7-bounties-from-5-alpha-beta-20261023/figures/compare.svg\" alt=\"Hard graph (10 × 10, long sequences): α × β\"></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>society</th>\n<th>frontier</th>\n<th>targets solved</th>\n<th>value gained</th>\n<th>ROI (value per spend)</th>\n<th>knowledge (bits)</th>\n<th>bits per money</th>\n<th>cost</th>\n<th>waste</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>1.8 ± 2.5</td>\n<td>0.4 ± 0.5</td>\n<td>26 ± 40</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.01</td>\n<td>133 ± 18</td>\n<td>0.022 ± 0.003</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>0.55 ± 0.03</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>α = 1, β = 0.25</td>\n<td>6.6 ± 0.8</td>\n<td>2.9 ± 1.2</td>\n<td>307 ±